{"name":"Chandra Cream","hex":"#ecba5d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The butterfat or milkfat part of milk which rises to the top; this part when separated from the remainder.","The liquid separated from milk, possibly with certain other milk products added, and with at least eighteen percent of it milkfat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cream-coloured; having a yellowish white colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chandra","blocks":[{"text":"Chandra, also known as Soma, is the Hindu god of the Moon, and is associated with the night, plants and vegetation. He is one of the Navagraha."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Chandra%2C_The_Moon_God%3B_Folio_from_a_Book_of_Dreams_LACMA_M.83.219.2_%282_of_3%29.jpg/330px-Chandra%2C_The_Moon_God%3B_Folio_from_a_Book_of_Dreams_LACMA_M.83.219.2_%282_of_3%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chandra"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Howling_at_the_Moon_in_Mississauga.jpg/500px-Howling_at_the_Moon_in_Mississauga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Howling_at_the_Moon_in_Mississauga.jpg/1280px-Howling_at_the_Moon_in_Mississauga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Howling_at_the_Moon_in_Mississauga.jpg/500px-Howling_at_the_Moon_in_Mississauga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The scriptures compare the Moon to a white goose in the blue lake of sky.[2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHowling_at_the_Moon_in_Mississauga.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/The_Moon_God_Chandra_%28possibly%29_in_His_Chariot_with_Wife_and_Attendant%2C_2nd-1st_century_BCE%2C_Shunga_period%2C_West_Bengal.jpg/500px-The_Moon_God_Chandra_%28possibly%29_in_His_Chariot_with_Wife_and_Attendant%2C_2nd-1st_century_BCE%2C_Shunga_period%2C_West_Bengal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/The_Moon_God_Chandra_%28possibly%29_in_His_Chariot_with_Wife_and_Attendant%2C_2nd-1st_century_BCE%2C_Shunga_period%2C_West_Bengal.jpg/1280px-The_Moon_God_Chandra_%28possibly%29_in_His_Chariot_with_Wife_and_Attendant%2C_2nd-1st_century_BCE%2C_Shunga_period%2C_West_Bengal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/The_Moon_God_Chandra_%28possibly%29_in_His_Chariot_with_Wife_and_Attendant%2C_2nd-1st_century_BCE%2C_Shunga_period%2C_West_Bengal.jpg/500px-The_Moon_God_Chandra_%28possibly%29_in_His_Chariot_with_Wife_and_Attendant%2C_2nd-1st_century_BCE%2C_Shunga_period%2C_West_Bengal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Possible depiction of the Moon God Chandra in his chariot with wife and attendant, 2nd-1st century BCE, Shunga period, West Bengal.[16]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Moon_God_Chandra_(possibly)_in_His_Chariot_with_Wife_and_Attendant%2C_2nd-1st_century_BCE%2C_Shunga_period%2C_West_Bengal.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Chandra_deva.jpg/330px-Chandra_deva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Chandra_deva.jpg/330px-Chandra_deva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chandra, British Museum, 13th century, Konark","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChandra_deva.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Milk-bottle.jpg/500px-Milk-bottle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Milk-bottle.jpg/500px-Milk-bottle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bottle of unhomogenised milk, with the cream clearly visible, resting on top of the milk","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMilk-bottle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/M